      "body": "### Redundant PATH forwarding in tmux session setup

**Low Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
`PATH` is included in the explicit `envArgs` forwarding list, but `NewTmuxSession` already unconditionally forwards `PATH` from `os.Getenv("PATH")` on every call (see `tmux.go` line 42). This results in PATH being set twice in the constructed shell command — once by the outer `env` and once by the inner `env`. Both resolve to the same value, so it's harmless but redundant and potentially confusing for future maintainers who may not realize `NewTmuxSession` already handles `PATH`.
